  "prefLabel": "Env-Or 303.04 National Fire Protection Association",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Or 303.04 National Fire Protection Association. The specified standards from the National Fire Protection Association (NFPA), 1 Batterymarch Park, Quincy, Massachusetts 02169-7471, (800) 344-3555, http://www.nfpa.org, shall apply as noted in the rules and summarized in Appendix B:\n\n(a) Subject to (b), below, the following NFPA standards shall apply:\n\n(1) NFPA 30 - “Flammable and Combustible Liquid Code” (NFPA 30);\n\n(2) NFPA 30A - “Code for Motor Fuel Dispensing Facilities and Repair Garages” (NFPA 30A);\n\n(3) NFPA 31 - “Standard for the Installation of Oil-Burning Equipment” (NFPA 31); and\n\n(4) NFPA 110 - “Standard for Emergency and Standby Power Systems” (NFPA 110).\n\n(b) The edition referenced by the state fire code as defined by RSA 153:1,VI-a shall apply, as reprinted in Appendix C.\n\nSource. (See Revision Note at chapter heading for Env-Or 300) #10487, eff 2-7-14; ss by #14094, eff 10-4-24",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-or300.html"
